Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fft: input scaling by shift, not division

VibeSDR patch for libxaac v0.1.14 (commit 2fbadd57; the decoder VibeServer links for xHE-AAC). Apache-2.0, as libxaac.
Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-29; applied in the order of xaac-patches/series by vibeserver/linux/build-libxaac.sh (Linux
and Mac). Every file it changes carries a "Modified by VibeSDR" notice (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). Measured with
xaacbench on the 7 ISO conformance streams, 12 xHE test streams (usac/xhe) and 4 off-air DAB+ unit logs, at PCM16 as
the server decodes, on arm64, armhf, ARMv6, i386 and amd64 (qemu) and the Mac. Instruction counts: qemu, guest
instructions per second of audio.

ixheaacd_complex_fft_p2_dec (and the armv7 C copy) scaled the input by xr[i] / (1 << shift) with a run-time shift: a
real division per sample. Replaced by the exact round-toward-zero shift. Bit-identical.

diff --git a/decoder/armv7/ixheaacd_fft_armv7.c b/decoder/armv7/ixheaacd_fft_armv7.c
index 37ea498..979925f 100644
--- a/decoder/armv7/ixheaacd_fft_armv7.c
+++ b/decoder/armv7/ixheaacd_fft_armv7.c
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+/* Modified by VibeSDR, 2026-10-29: the input scaling of
+ * ixheaacd_complex_fft_p2_armv7() divides by a power of two with a shift
+ * (rounding toward zero, as the division does) instead of a division per
+ * sample, a library call on 32-bit ARM. Identical results.
+ * Original: Copyright (C) 2018 The Android Open Source Project, Apache-2.0
+ * (see LICENSE and NOTICE). */
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 
@@ -38,9 +44,13 @@ VOID ixheaacd_complex_fft_p2_armv7(WORD32 *xr, WORD32 *xi, WORD32 nlength,
   else
     shift = ((n + 3) / 2);
 
-  for (i = 0; i < nlength; i++) {
-    ptr_x[2 * i] = (xr[i] / (1 << (shift)));
-    ptr_x[2 * i + 1] = (xi[i] / (1 << (shift)));
+  {
+    /* VibeSDR: x / 2^shift, rounding toward zero, without dividing */
+    const WORD32 vibe_bias = (WORD32)((1u << shift) - 1u);
+    for (i = 0; i < nlength; i++) {
+      ptr_x[2 * i] = (xr[i] + ((xr[i] >> 31) & vibe_bias)) >> shift;
+      ptr_x[2 * i + 1] = (xi[i] + ((xi[i] >> 31) & vibe_bias)) >> shift;
+    }
   }
 
   if (fft_mode == -1) {
